{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And you shall not take ransom for the life of a murderer.</b> This is a matter that was included in all punishments — and why did it come out? To teach you: for a murderer one does not take ransom, but for hand and foot and eye and tooth, and a burn, a wound, and a bruise, and other injuries, and for blemishes inflicted by the hand of Heaven, one does take ransom, as it is written: ״אם כופר יושת עליו״."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:47.276776165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}